<title>FRANCE: French bonds end higher on thin volume.</title>
<headline>French bonds end higher on thin volume.</headline>
<text>
<p>1540 GMT - French bonds end significantly higher but on low volumes as gains fuelled by a 1.6 pct drop in U.S. durable goods knock away key resistance in the last 10 minutes of pit trade. *Mar 10-yr future 129.30, up 0.30. Vol 15,536. High 129.32 *6.50 2006 OAT yield 5.71 pct vs 5.74. Bund spread -0.09. *Call money unch at 3-3/16 5/16. Mar PIBOR 96.69, up 0.01.</p>
</text>
